@startuml
!theme plain
title Oni frame dependencies - complete draft for review
start
:Main thread captures owned frame inputs\nworld identity, committed state, camera, settings;
:Render lane validates admission and source lifetime\nrejected / minimized work does not advance history;
partition "Stage A - scene submission" {
:Consume coherent terrain and particle publication\nresolve material ID16 + FP16 Kelvin per native cell;
:Rebuild full-domain visibility / jump acceleration;
:Prepare one RGB9E5 source per opaque native cell\nauthored + thermal emission + previous CH DC diffuse feedback\nempty / receive-only source cells are zero;
:Update coarse cascades L5 -> L1\none probe per 2x2 group, all directions\nhits read cached source; no BRDF or CH queries;
note right
  One persistent interval store per level.
  Barrier before dependent child reads.
  Unselected probes retain their old data.
end note
:Reconstruct every fine probe\nread current geometry + updated/retained cascades\nhits read cached source; CH only for own-probe EMA\noverwrite own CH record in place;
note right
  One field of 32-byte CH records.
  Source CH reads finish before fine writes.
  No history copy or raw-CH intermediate.
  Direction identity must match traced data.
end note
:Draw scene using updated CH and packed material/temperature grid\n4x MSAA at reduced raster extent\nalpha-blend CH-mean-lit gas before resolve;
}
:Confirmed A acceptance commits lighting phase, CH validity\nand active-presentation-time baseline;
partition "Stage B - reconstruction and post submission" {
:Hable temporal reconstruction\nread previous screen history, write next unexposed HDR\nS = ceil(R/2), B = 2*S, only R is valid;
:PostProcessPass: exposure / bloom / AgX\nconsume valid R only, produce display-linear R output;
}
:Confirmed B acceptance commits screen-history role, phase, camera\nand exposure state / timing;
partition "Stage C - presentation submission" {
:Nearest enlargement by fixed P, right/bottom crop to W\ndiagnostic inspection overlay, then native UI;
:Present actual surface and report presentation outcome;
}
note right
  All stages use the same ordered queue.
  Definite rejection commits nothing for that stage.
  Earlier accepted stages are never rolled back.
  Ambiguous submit quarantines resources and stops admission.
  No host wait between stages is implied.
end note
:Completion fences govern retirement and numeric-status inspection\nasync numeric failure stops new dependent work;
stop
@enduml
